While you're entitled to your opinion of course, and can put whatever
into your variant than you'd like, I'd have to disagree.  I think more
special rooms would be a great addition, so long as they weren't like
most of the rooms we have now, namely, a rectangular area filled with
theme monsters.

Think about how much shops, vaults and temples add to the game.
Especially shops.  More highly-programmatic additions to the dungeon
would be great.  Problem is, they aren't trivial to add, and it's
almost as hard to come up with a good idea for one as to add it.

Anyway, more special branches are also cool, but the thing about
special levels is that they're set-piece challenges in a game that
should always concern itself foremost with random generation.

